f_rule(int k) =>
    switch k
        0 => "Price falls into an H1 gap and turns. The turn leaves a small box on 5m. We wait at the edge of that box with a limit, like a goalkeeper on the line. HTF level: Price touches the H1 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Trail: After the first opposite candle, wait for a BC in profit, then move the stop to that pullback low / high. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        1 => "Same box-edge limit, at any UPG gap, only in the NY afternoon. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: Only take fills from 12:00 to 16:00 New York. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:3 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        2 => "Same box-edge limit at an M15 gap, only in the NY morning. HTF level: Price touches the M15 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: Only take fills from 09:30 to 12:00 New York. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        3 => "The NY afternoon makes its first range at 13:30–13:45. When price comes back to that low and turns, buyers defend it. We wait at the box edge. HTF level: Price touches the NY PM opening range low (13:30–13:45 New York) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:3 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        4 => "Session highs and lows are where stops sit. When price turns there in the H1 trend direction, we wait at the box edge. HTF level: Price touches the session or range high / low (Asia, London, pre-open, Globex, NY AM, NY PM) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: Trade only in the MMM PRO FVA H1 trend direction. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:3 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        5 => "An M15 internal box on the 1m chart, NY morning only, with a 20-point stop and no target. Few wins, but big ones. HTF level: Price touches the MMM PRO FVA M15 internal box for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 1m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: Only take fills from 09:30 to 12:00 New York. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: Fixed 20 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: No target: a runner. · Trail: After the first opposite candle, wait for a BC in profit, then move the stop to that pullback low / high. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        6 => "The LEZ is the last box before a break: the last place the winners loaded up. In London, when price comes back to it, we wait at the 1m box edge. HTF level: Price touches the MMM PRO FVA Bu / Be LEZ (M15 · H1 · H4) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 1m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Filter: Only take fills from 02:00 to 08:00 New York. · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: Fixed 20 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Trail: After the first opposite candle, wait for a BC in profit, then move the stop to that pullback low / high. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        7 => "The busiest strategy: any UPG gap, level held, limit at the 5m box edge. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Entry: Limit order at the reversal box edge: its top for longs, its bottom for shorts. The first touch fills. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Trail: After the first opposite candle, wait for a BC in profit, then move the stop to that pullback low / high. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        8 => "Price comes back to an H1 box, the retest only touches, and a BC closes out. We go with the H1 trend and move to BE after one BC. HTF level: Price touches the MMM PRO FVA H1 box (T#, P#, R#, internal, break box or LEZ) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Filter: Trade only in the MMM PRO FVA H1 trend direction. · Retest: Price comes back and touches the reversal box, but no candle closes inside it. · Entry: A BC closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:5 RR. · Trail: After 1 BC in profit, move the stop to entry. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        9 => "An LD is a break up. If the next 3 candles all stay outside the broken box, the break is real: like a door that stays open. We buy the 4th candle. Wait for: An LD: a 5m candle closes above the last bull box (a continuation break). · Then: Count the next 3 candles. None of them may close back inside the broken box. · Entry: Buy at the open of the 4th candle. · Stop: 1 tick past the broken box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the broken box: out at that close. · Target: 1:10 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        10 => "Same idea on 15m, both sides: the break stays outside for 3 candles, we join it. Wait for: An LD (long) or SD (short): a 15m candle closes past the last box in the trend direction. · Then: Count the next 3 candles. None of them may close back inside the broken box. · Entry: Enter at the open of the 4th candle. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Get out early: A candle closes back below the broken box (above it for shorts): out at that close. · Target: 1:10 RR. · Trail: After the first opposite candle, wait for a BC in profit, then move the stop to that pullback low / high. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        11 => "A 1-hour break up. We simply buy the next open and trail under each BC. Wait for: An LD: a 1h candle closes above the last bull box. · Entry: Buy at the open of the next 1h candle. · Stop: 1 tick past the broken box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A 1h candle closes back below the broken box. · Target: 1:5 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        12 => "Price falls into a gap, turns, and makes a 15m box. In Asia, price comes back and only wicks into the box. A BC closes out: we are in. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 15m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Filter: Only take entries from 18:00 to 02:00 New York. · Retest: Price comes back and only wicks into the box: no candle closes inside it. · Entry: A BC closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        13 => "The box needs 2 BCs to be trusted. Then price retests it, a BC closes out, and we buy the dip at 50% of that BC. HTF level: Price touches the H1 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. Then a 2nd BC must close in your direction before any retest. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Retest: Price comes back and touches the box. · Entry: A BC closes out of the box: place a limit at 50% of that BC. Cancel if price closes back past the box first. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 10 pts (ES 4 · gold 2.4 · crude 0.10), no cap. · Target: 1:10 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        14 => "Same as FVA.M14 on 15m at any UPG gap, in London, with a 50-point stop. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 15m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. Then a 2nd BC must close in your direction before any retest. · Filter: Only take entries from 02:00 to 08:00 New York. · Retest: Price comes back and only wicks into the box. · Entry: A BC closes out of the box: place a limit at 50% of that BC. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:3 RR. · Trail: Once in profit, move the stop under each new BC (over it for shorts). · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        15 => "Max’s own management: after the 1st BC in profit the stop goes to BE + fees. If we get shaken out and the box still holds, we re-enter on the next touch → BC. HTF level: Price touches the H1 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. Then a 2nd BC must close in your direction before any retest. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Retest: Price comes back and touches the box. · Entry: A BC closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: No target: a runner. · Manage: After the 1st BC in profit, move the stop to entry + 1 pt (fees). · Re-enter: Stopped or out at BE and the box still holds? Wait for touch → BC out again and re-enter. Up to 3 times. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        16 => "The cleanest one: price falls into a gap, turns, comes back and only wicks the box. The 1st BC back out of the box is the entry. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 15m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Retest: Price comes back and only wicks into the box: no candle closes inside it. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:3 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        17 => "Same retest. Then we wait at the high that the entry BC broke, with a small 20-point stop, and aim for 1:10. HTF level: Price touches the M15 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 15m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Retest: Price comes back and only wicks into the box. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: place a limit at the high it broke (low for shorts). · Stop: Fixed 20 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:10 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        18 => "A PRO FVA break box on the higher chart, a 5m box with an NBC inside, the retest, then the 1st BC out. Simple 1:2 target: easy for prop rules. HTF level: Price touches the MMM PRO FVA break box: CDL, CDS, LD or SD on M15 / H1 / H4 for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. The box must hold an NBC inside it (not BC on BC). · Retest: Price comes back and touches the box. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:2 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        19 => "Fast retests work best on 15m: the candle right after the break already touches the box. Then the 1st BC out is the entry. HTF level: Price touches the UPG gap (M15 · H1 · H4 · D · W) for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 15m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. The very next candle after the break candle is already the retest: no 2nd BC, NBC or opposite candle in between. · Filter: No candle closed through the level before the box printed (the level held). · Retest: The candle right after the break touches the box. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: 1 tick past the reversal box low (long) / high (short), at least 20 and at most 50 pts. · Get out early: A candle closes back below the reversal box (long) / above it (short): out at that close. · Target: 1:5 RR. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        20 => "After the break, a small NBC pauses the push. That pause usually brings price back to the box. Touch, 1st BC out, in. One re-entry allowed. HTF level: Price touches the M15 UPG gap for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 5m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. After the break candle, an NBC prints before price comes back to the box. · Retest: Price comes back and touches the box. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Target: 1:3 RR. · Re-enter: Stopped out and the box still holds? Wait for touch → BC out again and re-enter once. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."
        => "On 1m, price goes back and forth before the retest. After the entry, the stop goes to BE after 2 BCs, so full losses are rare. HTF level: Price touches the MMM PRO FVA M15 internal box for the first time. · Wait for: The first MMM PRO FVA reversal box in your direction prints on 1m: for longs a BuBC that closes above the last bearish candles, with the box low at or inside the level. Before the retest you see a 2nd BC, an NBC and an opposite BC. · Retest: Price comes back and a candle closes inside the box. · Entry: The 1st BC that closes out of the box: enter at the next open. · Stop: Fixed 50 pts (ES 20). · Target: 1:3 RR. · Trail: After 2 BCs in profit, move the stop to entry. · Time out: At the next session open (18:00 · 02:00 · 08:00 · 09:30 New York): losing → out at the open, winning → trail under each BC. Out at the 2nd session open."

f_num(array<string> a, int i) =>
    i < a.size() ? str.tonumber(a.get(i)) : na

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LEVELS ON THE CHART (nearest live levels, redrawn on the last candle)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var array<line>  LVL_L = array.new<line>()
var array<label> LVL_B = array.new<label>()
if barstate.islast
    for x in LVL_L
        line.delete(x)
    for x in LVL_B
        label.delete(x)
    LVL_L.clear()
    LVL_B.clear()
    if lvOn and RUN and LVS.size() > 0
        array<float> dist = array.new<float>()
        array<int>   idx  = array.new<int>()
        for i = 0 to LVS.size() - 1
            Lv v = LVS.get(i)
            if v.st != 9
                dist.push(v.st == 1 ? -1.0 : math.min(math.abs(close - v.top), math.abs(close - v.bot)))
                idx.push(i)
        int shown = 0
        while shown < lvN and dist.size() > 0
            int bj = 0
            for q = 0 to dist.size() - 1
                if dist.get(q) < dist.get(bj)
                    bj := q
            Lv v = LVS.get(idx.get(bj))
            dist.remove(bj)
            idx.remove(bj)
            color col = v.st == 1 ? EL_GOLD : v.d == 1 ? c_up : c_dn
            int x1 = v.t0
            int x2 = time + 15 * timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000
            LVL_L.push(line.new(x1, v.top, x2, v.top, xloc=xloc.bar_time, color=color.new(col, 30), width=1, style=line.style_dotted))
            if math.abs(v.top - v.bot) >= TICK / 2
                LVL_L.push(line.new(x1, v.bot, x2, v.bot, xloc=xloc.bar_time, color=color.new(col, 30), width=1, style=line.style_dotted))
            LVL_B.push(label.new(x2, v.d == 1 ? v.top : v.bot, (v.st == 1 ? "ARMED · " : "") + v.nm + (v.d == 1 ? " ▲" : " ▼"), xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left, color=color(na), textcolor=col, size=size.tiny))
            shown += 1

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TABLES · LIVE (what happens now) · STATISTICS (tested + this chart)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var table TL = na
var table TS = na
if barstate.isfirst
    if tlOn
        TL := table.new(f_pos(tlPos), 2, 12, bgcolor=EL_BG, frame_color=#3C3C3C, frame_width=1, border_color=#282828, border_width=1)
        table.merge_cells(TL, 0, 0, 1, 0)
    if tsOn
        TS := table.new(f_pos(tsPos), 7, 9, bgcolor=EL_BG, frame_color=#3C3C3C, frame_width=1, border_color=#282828, border_width=1)
        table.merge_cells(TS, 0, 0, 6, 0)
        table.merge_cells(TS, 0, 8, 6, 8)

f_c(table T, int c, int r, string tx, color tc, color bg, string z, string tip = "") =>
    table.cell(T, c, r, tx, text_color=tc, bgcolor=bg, text_halign=c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_left, text_size=f_tsz(z), tooltip=tip)
    true
f_lr(int r, string a, string b, color c, string tip = "") =>
    f_c(TL, 0, r, a, EL_LBL, r % 2 == 0 ? EL_ROW : EL_ALT, tbSz, tip)
    f_c(TL, 1, r, b, c, r % 2 == 0 ? EL_ROW : EL_ALT, tbSz)
    r + 1

if barstate.islast and tlOn
    table.clear(TL, 0, 1, 1, 11)
    table.cell(TL, 0, 0, "─ MMM EDGE PRO FVA · " + syminfo.ticker + " · " + str.format_time(time, "EEE HH:mm", NY) + " NY ─", text_color=EL_GOLD, bgcolor=EL_BG, text_size=f_tsz(tbSz))
    int r = 1
    r := f_lr(r, "Strategy", selIn, EL_GOLD, f_rule(K))
    string vd = MKT <= 0 ? "PASS" : str.split(f_mk(K, MKT), "|").get(1)
    r := f_lr(r, "Market", MKTN + " · " + (MKT < 0 ? "not tested: NQ rules" : MKT == 0 ? "PASS (strategy book)" : vd + " on its own data") + (MOK ? "" : " · OFF here (Market Check)"), MOK ? (MKT <= 0 or str.startswith(vd, "PASS") ? EL_POS : EL_WARN) : EL_WARN, "Market Check is " + (mkChk ? "ON" : "OFF") + ". Passed on ES: " + "FVA.M3, FVA.M19" + " · gold: " + "FVA.M13, FVA.M14, FVA.M16" + " · crude: " + "FVA.M13, FVA.M19" + ".")
    r := f_lr(r, "Chart", TFOK ? str.tostring(LTF) + (LTF == 60 ? "" : "m") + " chart ✔" : "use the " + (LTF == 60 ? "1h" : str.tostring(LTF) + "m") + " chart for " + CODE, TFOK ? EL_LBL : EL_WARN)
    r := f_lr(r, "Window", WA < 0 ? "any hour" + (H1F ? " · H1 trend " + (h1Side == 1 ? "▲" : h1Side == -1 ? "▼" : "—") : "") : (winNow ? "OPEN" : "closed") + " · " + str.format("{0}:{1}–{2}:{3} NY", str.tostring(int(WA / 60), "00"), str.tostring(WA % 60, "00"), str.tostring(int(WB / 60), "00"), str.tostring(WB % 60, "00")), WA < 0 or winNow ? EL_LBL : EL_MUTE)
    // what the strategy waits for now
    int nLv = 0
    int nArm = 0
    for v in LVS
        nLv += v.st == 9 ? 0 : 1
        nArm += v.st == 1 ? 1 : 0
    string now = ""
    color  nowC = EL_LBL
    int nTr = 0
    int nLim = 0
    int nSet = 0
    float uU = 0.0
    for s in SU
        if s.st == 3
            nTr += 1
            uU += ((close - s.E) * s.d - COST) * USD
        else if s.st == 2
            nLim += 1
        else if s.st != 9
            nSet += 1
    if not RUN
        now := not TFOK ? "off · wrong chart" : "off · not passed on " + MKTN
        nowC := EL_WARN
    else if nTr > 0
        now := str.tostring(nTr) + " trade" + (nTr > 1 ? "s" : "") + " open · " + (uU >= 0 ? "+" : "") + f_usd(uU)
        nowC := uU >= 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG
    else if nLim > 0
        now := str.tostring(nLim) + " limit order" + (nLim > 1 ? "s" : "") + " waiting"
        nowC := EL_GOLD
    else if nSet > 0
        now := TYP == 2 ? "LD / SD printed · waiting 3 candles outside the box" : str.tostring(nSet) + " reversal box" + (nSet > 1 ? "es" : "") + " · waiting for the retest → 1st BC out"
        nowC := EL_GOLD
    else if TYP == 2 or TYP == 3
        now := "waiting for a " + (SIDE == 1 ? "LD" : "LD / SD") + " on this chart"
    else if nArm > 0
        now := str.tostring(nArm) + " level" + (nArm > 1 ? "s" : "") + " touched · waiting for the reversal box (1 hour)"
        nowC := EL_GOLD
    else
        now := "waiting for a first touch · " + str.tostring(nLv) + " live level" + (nLv == 1 ? "" : "s")
    r := f_lr(r, "Now", now, nowC)
    r := f_lr(r, "Today", str.tostring(tdN) + " trade" + (tdN == 1 ? "" : "s") + " · " + str.tostring(tdW) + " ✔ " + str.tostring(tdL) + " ✖ · Net " + (tdU >= 0 ? "+" : "") + f_usd(tdU), tdN == 0 ? EL_MUTE : tdU >= 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG)
    r := f_lr(r, "Last", lastTx == "" ? "—" : lastTx, EL_LBL)
    r := f_lr(r, "This chart", rN == 0 ? "no trades yet" : str.tostring(rN) + " trades · WR " + str.tostring(100.0 * rW / rN, "#") + "% · avg RR " + f_sgn(rSum / rN, "#.00") + " · PF " + (rGL > 0 ? str.tostring(rGW / rGL, "#.00") : "—") + " · Net " + (rUsd >= 0 ? "+" : "") + f_usd(rUsd), rN == 0 ? EL_MUTE : rUsd >= 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG, "What the indicator traded on this chart's history, at your size, after costs. Max drawdown " + f_usd(-rDD) + " · max losses in a row " + str.tostring(rML) + ".")
    r := f_lr(r, "Size", str.tostring(szN) + " " + CTN + " · 1 pt = " + f_usd(USD) + " · cost " + str.tostring(COST) + " pts a trade", EL_MUTE)

if barstate.islast and tsOn
    string z = tbSz
    table.cell(TS, 0, 0, "─ " + selIn + " · tested numbers · " + (MKT <= 0 ? "NQ" : MKTN) + " ─", text_color=EL_GOLD, bgcolor=EL_BG, text_size=f_tsz(z), tooltip=f_rule(K))
    array<string> hd = array.from("", "Trades", "WR (win rate)", "avg RR", "PF", "t-score", "Losses in a row")
    for c = 0 to 6
        f_c(TS, c, 1, hd.get(c), EL_GOLD, EL_ROW, z)
    array<string> nq = str.split(f_nq(K), "|")
    array<string> p1 = str.split(nq.get(0), ",")
    array<string> p2 = str.split(nq.get(1), ",")
    array<string> ba = str.split(nq.get(2), ",")
    f_c(TS, 0, 2, "NQ period 1 · 2022–25", EL_LBL, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 1, 2, p1.get(0), EL_LBL, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 2, 2, p1.get(1) + "%", EL_LBL, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 3, 2, f_sgn(f_num(p1, 2), "#.00"), f_num(p1, 2) > 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 4, 2, "—", EL_MUTE, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 5, 2, p1.get(3), EL_LBL, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 6, 2, "—", EL_MUTE, EL_ALT, z)
    f_c(TS, 0, 3, "NQ period 2 · MNQ 2026", EL_LBL, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 1, 3, p2.get(0), EL_LBL, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 2, 3, p2.get(1) + "%", EL_LBL, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 3, 3, f_sgn(f_num(p2, 2), "#.00"), f_num(p2, 2) > 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 4, 3, "—", EL_MUTE, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 5, 3, p2.get(3), EL_LBL, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 6, 3, "—", EL_MUTE, EL_ROW, z)
    f_c(TS, 0, 4, "NQ both periods ✔ PASS", EL_POS, EL_ALT, z)
    for c = 1 to 6
        string v = ba.get(c - 1)
        f_c(TS, c, 4, c == 2 ? v + "%" : c == 3 ? f_sgn(str.tonumber(v), "#.00") : v, c == 3 ? (str.tonumber(v) > 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG) : EL_LBL, EL_ALT, z)
    // the other markets (rebuilt engine, both periods)
    for m = 1 to 3
        array<string> mm = str.split(f_mk(K, m), "|")
        array<string> a = str.split(mm.get(0), ",")
        string nmM = m == 1 ? "ES" : m == 2 ? "Gold" : "Crude"
        string vv = mm.get(1)
        color bgc = m % 2 == 1 ? EL_ROW : EL_ALT
        f_c(TS, 0, 4 + m, nmM + " · " + vv, str.startswith(vv, "PASS") ? EL_POS : EL_WARN, bgc, z, "Rebuilt FVA test engine on " + nmM + "'s own data, Dec 2025 – Oct 2026 (1m / 5m charts: fewer months), both periods together.")
        if a.size() < 6
            f_c(TS, 1, 4 + m, "no trades", EL_MUTE, bgc, z)
            for c = 2 to 6
                f_c(TS, c, 4 + m, "", EL_MUTE, bgc, z)
        else
            for c = 1 to 6
                string v = a.get(c - 1)
                f_c(TS, c, 4 + m, c == 2 ? v + "%" : c == 3 ? f_sgn(str.tonumber(v), "#.00") : v, c == 3 ? (str.tonumber(v) > 0 ? EL_POS : EL_NEG) : EL_LBL, bgc, z)
    table.cell(TS, 0, 8, "WR = win rate · avg RR = average result per trade (1 = one stop) · PF = money won ÷ money lost · t-score 2+ = probably not luck · PASS = made money in both periods · research only, not advice", text_color=EL_MUTE, bgcolor=EL_BG, text_size=f_tsz(z), text_halign=text.align_left)
